00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:52.700
Basically, the funny story here between Sakamoto and Iwata is like Yokoi would come down, play the game in front of both of them.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:55.440
Just be, you know, not a single word was said.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:03:00.440
He'd just get up and then he would say all of his thoughts and leave and just expect for, you know,

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:02.560
it's going to take them a couple of days to make these changes.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.140
But Iwata is like a programming genius.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:10.700
You know, he knows how to program and he knows the NES hardware specifically.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.780
He programmed certain changes for that.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.800
They asked for in the game in just minutes, you know, and that was like unheard.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:24.800
Like Yokoi was able to be in the room, watch Iwata make the changes and put put them out on a new version for him to test.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.620
That's ridiculous. It's crazy.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:35.680
And then the other thing I learned from this, this is all from a developer interview with Sakamoto during a like Nintendo.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:39.780
It was like during an Iwata asks, essentially, where like they have interviews.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:44.960
Iwata used to do them with each person who made the games when they were going over these past Nintendo games.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:48.640
Really cool. I hope Nintendo continues that, even though Iwata is no longer with us.

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:50.360
