00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:16.050
I don't think it's like Kung Fu where you're going to die in the first level 15 times before

00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:17.050
you get to the second floor.

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:21.830
Right. Um, I think it's more of like a guitar, like where it's, it's got a low barrier of entry,

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:23.010
but a really high ceiling.

00:14:23.330 --> 00:14:24.210
You know what I mean? Yeah.

00:14:24.550 --> 00:14:28.270
And I think one place where we see that most is in Balloon Trip.

00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:39.770
Yeah. That is the game C.

00:14:39.930 --> 00:14:43.650
We'll go back to the one player game in a bit when we talk about two

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:46.570
player, but I thought we should talk about Balloon Trip because it's another one player version

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:52.030
of the game. Essentially, this is a side scrolling game where the screen keeps moving, but you have

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:53.430
to collect just the balloons.

00:14:53.550 --> 00:14:59.030
There's no real enemies or anything except for the lightning bolts, which are sometimes

00:14:59.030 --> 00:15:00.790
static, sometimes moving patterns.

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:03.090
But the balloons are the only thing you have to collect.

00:15:03.330 --> 00:15:08.630
And there's like a rank thing up at the top right that says like rank 50 and then counts

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:10.170
down. Anybody know what that's about?

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:14.150
I have no idea. The 40 something imaginary players that you're playing with.

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:16.810
Yeah. It's like, yeah, they're way ahead of you.

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:19.270
Yeah. They're way ahead of you.

00:15:20.170 --> 00:15:21.410
Joe, did you play Balloon Trip?

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:25.810
Yeah. I was my one, I guess, complaint about it.

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:28.210
Maybe I'm just being a baby is that you only get one life.

00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:31.750
So I felt like I felt like you have to start from scratch after that one life.

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:33.750
So I felt like I never got to get that far.

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:35.690
So I guess it's a set up to get good at it.

00:15:35.690 --> 00:15:37.990
No, I mean, you get hit once.

00:15:38.190 --> 00:15:41.650
You start with two balloons, but you get hit once and you're dead, which is weird because

00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:42.470
they're all lightning bolts. Yeah.

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:47.130
It's kind of cool, though, because it goes back into that expert rewarding thing.

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:50.590
And this is sort of like a training program for the rest of the game.

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:53.350
Like if you don't want to, if you feel like you're not good enough for the rest of the

00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:57.130
game, but you just want to focus on flying better, which will make you better at the

00:15:57.130 --> 00:15:59.150
game, then you can just jump into this one.

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:04.630
Right. Yeah. And to your point, too, about like the expert thing, it's like in Balloon Trip, it's always the

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:05.710
same layout, too.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:11.670
So one thing that was funny is I was watching something of Iwata playing the game when he's

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:15.930
the president of Nintendo of America years later on like a Game Center CX thing that's

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:16.810
like a show in Japan.

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:20.710
And, you know, they ask him like, oh, when was the last time you played this game?

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:22.950
And he was like, I play this game pretty often.

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:28.290
And then he goes into Balloon Trip mode and he like has like the perfect pattern of like

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:33.250
going through this thing and like starts going up, dips down low, comes back up.

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:34.730
He knows where the fish is going to be.

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:36.850
It's really funny to watch that happen.

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:39.110
And that's what I imagine an expert playing like.

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:44.710
Now, does anybody know what happens if you collect 20 balloons in Balloon Trip in a row

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:45.750
without missing any?

00:16:46.210 --> 00:16:47.070
No. Good. No.

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:49.930
I'm glad no one knew because it's a very hard thing to pull off.

00:16:49.930 --> 00:16:51.910
Personally, I'll just be honest.

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:53.510
I have not been able to do it myself.

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:59.430
It's very hard to get 20 balloons in a row while dodging all those lightning bolts and

00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:01.790
also like, you know, not missing any at the same time.

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:07.450
So what happens is if you do magic like 20, the balloons turn orange and they kind of freeze

00:17:07.450 --> 00:17:11.610
for a second. So you're able to collect like a bunch of them before the stage continues.

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:13.870
Oh, OK, cool. I think it's like a neat little thing.

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:18.790
It kind of reminds me of how pinball after like doing a certain task, the board would change

00:17:18.790 --> 00:17:21.750
colors. That's another thing that he want to program.

00:17:21.950 --> 00:17:25.350
So it seemed like he just had a flair for like, do these funny things and I'll change

00:17:25.350 --> 00:17:26.390
the colors of the game.

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:27.470
He likes colors.

00:17:28.510 --> 00:17:29.870
Well, you know how simple they are, Sean.

00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:31.310
We were talking about that earlier in the interviews.

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:32.770
They're like, I like colors.

00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:35.410
Yeah. They're like, we wanted to make a game that was about colors.

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:39.590
Colors are good. They never said that in an interview.

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:40.930
I just want to put that out there.

