00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:16.690
But it doesn't feel as rewarding as getting a higher score in the one player mode because it's the same thing over and over again.

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:19.590
I found myself keep dying at the same points.

00:18:19.730 --> 00:18:21.750
And it has like that frustration value.

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:23.730
You're just like, OK, again, again, again.

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:26.370
But after a while, I was just like, I think I've seen this.

00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:39.490
Yeah. You know, like if there was maybe some different kind of variety, like each stage was randomly generated or later on enemies got added or the fish started like hopping out and trying to swallow you.

00:18:39.810 --> 00:18:41.750
Like, I feel like that stuff would be cool.

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:43.490
But there wasn't enough going on.

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:47.450
It was just more like, you know, dodging the lightning bolts was the only thing.

00:18:47.630 --> 00:18:48.790
It's going right back to Flappy Bird.

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:51.570
And this is like this mode is the Flappy Bird mode.

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:53.890
Right. That's pretty accurate, actually.

00:18:54.110 --> 00:19:00.950
It almost just feels like like you could you would just use this as like you're playing this game with a friend and you have like five more minutes.

00:19:01.050 --> 00:19:04.890
You're like, let's see who can get farther because you're probably not going to be in unless you're really good at it.

00:19:05.130 --> 00:19:07.170
It's not going to take that long before one of you dies.

00:19:07.610 --> 00:19:11.770
Right. And speaking of friends, that was a great segue for the two player mode.

00:19:11.970 --> 00:19:12.950
I love friends.

