00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:41.370
So I played very recently.

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:47.770
And it's it's definitely better as a two player experience, I think, because it's a little more, you know,

00:19:47.770 --> 00:19:49.190
you can screw each other over.

00:19:49.310 --> 00:19:50.930
You're trying to get it's the same thing.

00:19:51.050 --> 00:19:52.850
You're just trying to get more points than the other person.

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:55.230
But you can also pop each other's balloons now.

00:19:55.430 --> 00:20:02.790
So the floaty controls combined with like the frantic nature of it all makes it kind of an interesting competitive, competitive experience.

00:20:02.790 --> 00:20:09.690
And even when you're not trying to be competitive, you still run that risk of popping your, you know, your friend's balloon.

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:13.010
Like you're not trying to do it, but, you know, you're both trying to go after this enemy.

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:16.610
And then all of a sudden it's like you pop their balloon and it's like, oh, well, I'm sorry.

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:17.830
I didn't mean it. Yeah.

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:28.530
Damn it, Mike. Mike and I played a couple of times and that seemed to be the case for most of it is, I mean, a lot of times it's just beneficial to for both of you to not screw each other over.

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:34.590
I would say I would agree with that and I would say even more so in this game, we talked about this in Mario Brothers where Sean was not having it.

00:20:34.870 --> 00:20:37.110
He's like, no, you got to kill each other in this game.

00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:38.690
It's all about the points.

00:20:38.890 --> 00:20:49.250
In this game, the points are king still, but I think you get more points when you keep your second player alive and you help each other than you would ever get on your own.

00:20:49.410 --> 00:20:51.270
Because also when you divide and conquer.

00:20:51.490 --> 00:20:57.350
You'll get more points, but you like you still run the risk of like, and I did this and I was playing with you.

00:20:57.350 --> 00:21:03.130
So I knew that you kept getting more, but like I was trying to be I was trying to be cooperative for once.

00:21:03.390 --> 00:21:06.490
Yeah. So you're still running that risk of falling behind.

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:08.130
Yeah. While someone else gets.

00:21:08.270 --> 00:21:09.650
And yeah, that does happen.

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:18.950
I think even though we were both doing pretty good, we were both at 200,000 and you were still like, you know, it was like when I had 220, you had 200, you know?

00:21:19.070 --> 00:21:22.350
So it's like even though we thought we were close, it was a 20,000 point difference.

00:21:22.570 --> 00:21:24.970
Quite the difference. And I didn't mean to brag about that.

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:27.970
I'm talking about it because we're talking about the multiplayer section.

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:37.930
All right. So we talked about two player.

