You know, you could maybe say that, but I'm not saying that balloon kid is actually like the Game Boy sequel to this game.

00:21:51.430 --> 00:22:01.330
Oh, and what's interesting about that, I wouldn't even think to bring it up really, because there's been other Game Boy ports of the games that we played on NES so far, like baseball and stuff like that.

00:22:01.850 --> 00:22:06.570
But game balloon kid is interesting because it's not a port.

00:22:06.690 --> 00:22:10.330
It's a sequel. And it's actually like a platform adventure game.

00:22:10.470 --> 00:22:12.090
But you still have balloons tied to your body.

00:22:12.290 --> 00:22:13.450
You still have balloons tied to your body.

00:22:13.590 --> 00:22:17.070
There are stages and levels, like totally different, totally new.

00:22:17.270 --> 00:22:19.390
And you're collecting balloons still.

00:22:19.550 --> 00:22:25.630
But there's like platforming challenges and you have to like, you know, complete a mission.

00:22:25.930 --> 00:22:28.870
You know, there's a there's an actual like structure to the game.

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:30.810
That sounds cool. And yeah, it's very interesting.

00:22:31.090 --> 00:22:37.110
Is it an Nevada game? It's somehow ringing a bell to me like I don't I don't know this game, but it's when you're the way you're describing it.

00:22:37.170 --> 00:22:38.790
I feel like I've seen it or played it before.

