I think it was right around, like, probably 160, 170 was my best.

00:27:52.110 --> 00:27:53.590
Okay. But you're still overachieving.

00:27:53.790 --> 00:27:54.790
Still. Well, you know what?

00:27:54.870 --> 00:27:55.770
I will say this.

00:27:55.990 --> 00:27:58.690
This is similar to how, like, I played a lot of golf.

00:27:59.110 --> 00:28:00.610
Yeah. I played a lot of Balloon Fight.

00:28:00.850 --> 00:28:01.930
I really like this game.

00:28:02.110 --> 00:28:08.030
And, speaking of talking about whether we like or dislike this game, it's time for The Essential Games List.

00:28:11.030 --> 00:28:12.070
All right, guys.

00:28:13.090 --> 00:28:15.430
We took a quick break there to listen to Sam's music.

00:28:15.830 --> 00:28:17.490
This is The Essential Games List.

00:28:17.570 --> 00:28:21.090
And if you're unfamiliar, go listen to some other episodes.

00:28:21.330 --> 00:28:23.770
No, I'm joking. Seriously, listen to some of the other episodes.

00:28:24.250 --> 00:28:31.290
The Essential Games List is where we kind of determine, like, you know, you got all these games out today and your backlog is getting bigger and bigger.

00:28:31.290 --> 00:28:33.450
But, hey, there's these games on the NES.

00:28:33.550 --> 00:28:35.710
Are they any good? Are they essential even?

00:28:35.710 --> 00:28:36.930
We're going to talk about that.

00:28:37.030 --> 00:28:39.010
But we're not talking about if they were good then.

00:28:39.330 --> 00:28:42.850
That's kind of like history has decided if these games were good back then.

00:28:42.850 --> 00:28:45.390
We're deciding if they're still good today.

00:28:45.750 --> 00:28:48.610
So, with that in mind, Sean, Balloon Fight.

00:28:51.790 --> 00:28:53.230
Sean needs a moment.

00:28:54.370 --> 00:28:55.830
Yeah, he had a tough time earlier.

00:28:55.990 --> 00:28:56.990
So, we'll move over to Sam.

00:28:57.170 --> 00:28:58.770
Sam, Balloon Fight.

00:28:59.150 --> 00:29:00.050
What'd you think?

00:29:00.230 --> 00:29:01.490
Would you still play it today?

00:29:01.670 --> 00:29:04.510
Balloon Fight. I think that it is a solid game.

00:29:04.770 --> 00:29:06.790
I think that it's a fun game.

00:29:07.190 --> 00:29:09.530
It's a fun game, you know, with people, like, with friends.

00:29:09.530 --> 00:29:14.110
It's great. I think that it's a game that has lots of layers that you don't usually see.

00:29:14.410 --> 00:29:17.930
But it's still not, like, I wouldn't say it's essential.

00:29:18.190 --> 00:29:19.890
I think that it's a ton of fun.

00:29:20.330 --> 00:29:23.390
More if you have friends to play with, it's a ton of fun.

00:29:23.570 --> 00:29:25.290
But, no, it's not essential.

00:29:25.470 --> 00:29:27.390
Okay. This is just something I've noticed.

00:29:27.530 --> 00:29:30.350
I love when you know that we like a game.

00:29:30.530 --> 00:29:31.650
Like, we would recommend it.

00:29:31.650 --> 00:29:32.610
We wouldn't say it's essential.

00:29:32.990 --> 00:29:35.270
When we do the whole praise thing and then say, but.

00:29:35.730 --> 00:29:38.390
Yeah. Yeah, because I can't just be like, oh, no, it's not essential.

00:29:38.530 --> 00:29:40.610
You know, I feel like I'd be a jerk if I did that.

00:29:40.610 --> 00:29:41.710
Right, right. Because it is fun.

00:29:41.790 --> 00:29:44.010
And you can tell there's a lot of love put into this game.

00:29:44.290 --> 00:29:48.610
Yep. Joe? I can't imagine someone picking up this game and not liking it.

00:29:48.950 --> 00:29:50.570
It is kind of like what Sam said.

00:29:50.650 --> 00:29:51.530
It is really fun.

00:29:52.970 --> 00:29:57.250
The controls and it being a two-player game makes it, like, a good game when you have company over.

00:29:57.990 --> 00:29:59.530
But, overall. Yeah.

00:30:00.250 --> 00:30:05.210
Overall, I think one thing we didn't really mention was that it is, once you kind of get

00:30:05.210 --> 00:30:06.510
into it, it is kind of bare bones.

00:30:06.750 --> 00:30:09.150
It doesn't, I can see it getting old fast.

00:30:09.570 --> 00:30:10.670
So, yeah.

00:30:10.710 --> 00:30:13.310
I mean, it's definitely a play it, in my opinion.

00:30:13.530 --> 00:30:14.950
But I wouldn't vote for it to be essential.

00:30:15.350 --> 00:30:17.170
Okay. Sean, you ready for us?

00:30:17.330 --> 00:30:18.130
I'm ready for you.

00:30:18.310 --> 00:30:26.470
Let me hear it. See, I'm trying to think of the other games that we've played so far and how often I'm

00:30:26.470 --> 00:30:27.590
ever going to play those again.

00:30:27.950 --> 00:30:29.570
And a lot of them are never.

00:30:29.970 --> 00:30:32.750
Yeah. And I think about Balloon Fight.

00:30:32.950 --> 00:30:36.950
And I think about what kind of games are like Balloon Fight now.

00:30:37.090 --> 00:30:38.430
And there aren't that many.

00:30:38.850 --> 00:30:40.530
Like, there's Joust.

00:30:40.910 --> 00:30:43.930
Mm-hmm. In terms of just the way that you play.

00:30:43.950 --> 00:30:45.970
And that's also a very old game.

00:30:46.430 --> 00:30:50.250
I would say that I think this is an essential game.

00:30:50.370 --> 00:30:52.190
Okay. For the NES, yes.

00:30:52.630 --> 00:30:56.750
Sean, there was one thing that you focused in on there that I was definitely going to

00:30:56.750 --> 00:30:57.990
say, so I'm going to say it again.

00:30:58.430 --> 00:31:01.750
There is not another game like this today.

00:31:02.170 --> 00:31:08.330
Like, this is a game that you can still play and has not been, like, reiterated a thousand

00:31:08.330 --> 00:31:13.710
times. I think it is good old-fashioned fun that I think you could pick up and play today.

00:31:14.010 --> 00:31:18.390
In fact, this is the kind of game that makes me wish there was virtual console on Switch,

00:31:18.390 --> 00:31:23.350
even though we all know how easy it is to get a Raspberry Pi and play these games.

00:31:23.510 --> 00:31:27.350
I would love to have this game on Switch so that I could easily just break out the Joy-Cons,

00:31:27.570 --> 00:31:30.570
play with a second player right then and there anywhere in the world.

00:31:30.710 --> 00:31:34.870
Like, you know, a game like baseball or a game like even we were talking earlier about

00:31:34.870 --> 00:31:39.170
Kung Fu, those games don't really make me crave virtual console on Switch because I'm

00:31:39.170 --> 00:31:40.810
like, oh, well, you know, I can play those, you know.

00:31:40.970 --> 00:31:43.610
This is a game where I would want to have, like, oh, hey, I have Balloon Fight on me.

00:31:43.650 --> 00:31:45.770
You want to get, like, a quick round in before this movie starts?

00:31:45.770 --> 00:31:49.190
Like, that's weird and, like, sounds like a Nintendo commercial.

00:31:49.490 --> 00:31:51.470
But that's kind of, like, how I use my Switch.

00:31:51.650 --> 00:31:54.450
Like, I use it in, like, rare moments where I'm like, hey, I just happen to have this out

00:31:54.450 --> 00:31:58.770
and you want to play it now? I'm not a guy who, like, plays his Switch too much in his alone time.

00:31:58.770 --> 00:31:59.990
I like to play it with friends.

00:32:00.130 --> 00:32:03.790
Yeah. You know, so this is a game where I was like, oh, I kind of wish this was on the Switch

00:32:03.790 --> 00:32:04.930
and this would be a great use of it.

00:32:05.790 --> 00:32:09.970
That said, obviously, that means that I think that this game is still worth playing today.

00:32:10.370 --> 00:32:12.370
And I'm going to put it on the Essential Games list.

00:32:12.770 --> 00:32:13.890
It's on the Essential Games list.

00:32:13.890 --> 00:32:16.470
So it is an Essential game.

00:32:16.630 --> 00:32:21.130
Yeah. And that's, you know, what's funny is I knew I was going to vote at Essential days ago.

00:32:21.190 --> 00:32:25.290
But it's good that I finally was getting somebody else on board for it too.

00:32:25.910 --> 00:32:27.610
Joe, how do you feel about it being Essential?

00:32:28.010 --> 00:32:31.930
I actually, I still stand by, you know, my opinion.

00:32:32.130 --> 00:32:34.950
But it's not one where I'm opposed to it being Essential.

00:32:34.950 --> 00:32:40.030
I mean, this is the closest one for me to being Essential that we had in a long time.

00:32:41.050 --> 00:32:47.890
So I'd like to say it's not, but it doesn't upset me that it is because it's a good game.

00:32:48.030 --> 00:32:49.010
That's really cool.

00:32:49.550 --> 00:32:51.750
And so, yeah, I think, you know, this is a fun way.

00:32:51.850 --> 00:32:55.130
And who knows, you know, we will talk about this at the end of 86.

00:32:55.210 --> 00:33:00.450
This could wind up being an Excitebike situation where we're just really jazzed about this game

00:33:00.450 --> 00:33:05.010
right now, but then the end of 86 party comes up and I'm like, I haven't played this game since.

00:33:05.010 --> 00:33:07.070
So I don't know if I actually liked it.

